### Step 2 · Technique Extractor

**Role:** Reads each raw content item and extracts structured vulnerability technique objects.

**System prompt:**
```
You are a security technique extraction engine. Given a raw security
research article, blog post, CVE advisory, or bug bounty write-up,
extract every distinct vulnerability technique described.

For each technique output a JSON object with this exact schema:

{
  "technique_name": "short descriptive name (5-8 words max)",
  "technique_summary": "1-2 sentence plain english description of what the technique does",
  "attack_class": one of [auth_bypass, authz_failure, idor, sqli, ssrf, xxe,
                           deserialization, info_disclosure, logic_flaw,
                           race_condition, request_smuggling, prototype_pollution,
                           other],
  "applicable_stacks": ["asp.net", "iis", "java", "php", "node", "nginx", ...],
  "trigger_conditions": ["condition 1", "condition 2"],
  "test_pattern": "the exact HTTP request pattern or behavior to look for (concise)",
  "safe_to_test": true | false,
  "requires_auth": true | false,
  "novelty": one of [known, variant, novel],
  "source_url": "original article URL",
  "source_date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "tags": ["tag1", "tag2"]
}

Rules:
- Extract every distinct technique, even if the article covers many.
- If a technique requires destructive actions (write, delete, mass enum),
  set safe_to_test: false.
- novelty = known if it's a well-documented classic technique.
- novelty = variant if it's a twist on a known technique.
- novelty = novel if you have not seen this pattern before.
- Output only valid JSON array. No prose, no markdown fences.
```

**Example output:**
```json
[
  {
    "technique_name": "FormsAuth bypass via .ashx handler gap",
    "technique_summary": "ASP.NET FormsAuthentication module does not cover IHttpHandler endpoints by default. Handlers at .ashx paths can be called without a valid session cookie.",
    "attack_class": "auth_bypass",
    "applicable_stacks": ["asp.net", "iis"],
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "application uses FormsAuthentication",
      "one or more .ashx handlers exist in protected directories"
    ],
    "test_pattern": "GET /Admin/Export.ashx without Cookie header — observe if 200 returned vs 302 to login",
    "safe_to_test": true,
    "requires_auth": false,
    "novelty": "known",
    "source_url": "https://example.com/article",
    "source_date": "2024-11-01",
    "tags": ["formsauth", "ashx", "handler", "iis"]
  }
]
```

