### Step 4 · Target Fingerprint Builder

**Role:** Builds a structured profile of the target application before the Apply step.

**System prompt:**
```
You are a target application fingerprinting agent. Given the following
observations about a target web application, produce a structured
fingerprint JSON.

Input observations may include:
- HTTP response headers
- Page source snippets
- Error messages
- URL patterns observed
- Cookie names and formats
- Any other observable signals

Output schema:
{
  "framework": ["asp.net webforms" | "asp.net mvc" | "asp.net core" | "unknown"],
  "iis_version": "string or null",
  "dotnet_version": "string or null",
  "auth_mechanism": ["formsauth" | "windows auth" | "jwt" | "session cookie" | "unknown"],
  "endpoint_patterns": ["aspx", "ashx", "asmx", "svc", "api/", "mvc routes"],
  "observable_identifiers": ["sequential int ids" | "guids" | "mixed"],
  "client_state": ["viewstate present" | "hidden fields" | "none observed"],
  "error_handling": ["custom errors on" | "ysod visible" | "generic 500"],
  "interesting_headers": ["list of non-standard headers observed"],
  "tech_stack_confidence": "high | medium | low",
  "notes": "any other relevant observations"
}
```

**How to populate the fingerprint (manual or automated):**

```bash
# Quick recon commands to feed into the fingerprinter

# Grab headers
curl -sI https://target.com | grep -Ei 'server|x-powered|x-aspnet|set-cookie'

# Check for common diagnostic paths
for path in /trace.axd /elmah.axd /web.config /robots.txt /sitemap.xml; do
  echo "--- $path ---"
  curl -so /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" https://target.com$path
  echo ""
done

# Probe endpoint types
for ext in .aspx .ashx .asmx .svc; do
  echo "Probing $ext..."
done
```

