## Knowledge Base Schema

Store each technique as a vector-embedded document with these metadata fields for filtering:

```python
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "technique_name": str,
  "technique_summary": str,        # embed this field
  "attack_class": str,             # filter
  "applicable_stacks": list[str],  # filter
  "trigger_conditions": list[str], # embed
  "test_pattern": str,             # embed
  "safe_to_test": bool,            # filter
  "novelty": str,                  # filter / sort
  "source_url": str,
  "source_date": date,             # sort / recency boost
  "tags": list[str],               # filter
  "times_applied": int,            # increment when used
  "confirmed_findings": int,       # increment on confirmed vuln
  "hit_rate": float                # confirmed_findings / times_applied
}
```

**Retrieval query for Step 5:**
```python
# Pseudo-code
results = kb.query(
    vector=embed(target_fingerprint_summary),
    filter={
        "applicable_stacks": {"$in": target.framework + target.endpoint_patterns},
        "safe_to_test": True,
        "attack_class": {"$in": relevant_classes_for_target}
    },
    sort=[
        ("novelty", DESC),       # novel techniques first
        ("source_date", DESC),   # recent first
        ("hit_rate", DESC)       # proven techniques up
    ],
    top_k=30  # feed top 30 to Step 5 for re-ranking
)
```

